nodecode-obscurify is a rewrite of Obscurify-ai's Obscurify-ai/hermes-obscurify-provider:
https://github.com/Obscurify-ai/hermes-obscurify-provider
commit 72ce6f5cf6d297c01d23198a84c21b561fa0698c
MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 Obscurify.ai (LICENSE)

Rewritten: the provider profile (its base of https://obscurify.ai/v1, its
OBSCURIFY_API_KEY variable, its signup address and its OpenAI-compatible chat
wire) as a Nodecode catalog row, the public /v1/models read that builds the
model list and each model's context window, the filter that leaves decision
models and models under the 64K floor out of the picker (the floor is the
section's min_context_tokens now), the featured fallback list with the
capabilities the original checked for it, and the reasoning_effort mapping --
Nodecode's `off' goes out as the API's `none'.

Added, because Nodecode's catalog is where a picker reads its list: the
catalog read runs once at start and hourly after that (the original read on
the first listing and cached for an hour), and a failed read leaves the list
already read standing.

Left out, and why: the Hermes private seams the original imported
(providers.base, ProviderProfile, register_provider) have no place here, so the
profile is a catalog row and its two methods (fetch_models,
get_model_context_length) are one catalog read and the rows it builds. Its
EFFORTS table carried an `ultra' rung above `max' that its API mapped to
`max'; Nodecode's ladder ends at `max', so the entry has nothing to map. The
utm_source=hermes tag on its signup address is a referral marker, and this
rewrite does not carry one.
